Features: SDD

Purpose:
  Feature planning, decision, and layer assignment system.
  Analyzes project state, evaluates new features, and assigns
  work to appropriate layers (L0-L4).

Owns: ./

Layers:
  L0:
    Name: MVP Core
    Description: Minimum viable product features, already implemented
    WorkMode: Maintenance only

  L1:
    Name: Customer Features
    Description: Features requested after MVP
    WorkMode: Implementation
    Priority: HIGH

  L2:
    Name: Enhancements
    Description: Performance improvements, UX enhancements
    WorkMode: Implementation
    Priority: MEDIUM

  L3:
    Name: Scalability
    Description: Scaling, multi-tenant, advanced security
    WorkMode: Implementation
    Priority: LOW

  L4:
    Name: Innovation
    Description: Experimental features, AI/ML, advanced analytics
    WorkMode: Research and POC

Rules:
  [FTR1] Features MUST be assigned to a layer (L0-L4).
  [FTR2] Work MUST proceed from L0 -> L1 -> L2 -> L3 -> L4.
  [FTR3] L0 MUST be stable before L1 work begins.
  [FTR4] L1 features MUST be approved by human before implementation.
  [FTR5] Layer assignment MUST be documented in decisions/.
  [FTR6] Features MAY span multiple layers if justified.
  [FTR7] Every feature decision MUST be traceable to its source.
  [FTR8] Human approval REQUIRED for L1+ features.
  [FTR9] L0 features MAY be implemented without approval if within scope.

DecisionProcess:
  1. Evaluate feature against current project state
  2. Assign feature to appropriate layer
  3. Identify affected components
  4. Create decision record (DEC-XXX)
  5. Create tasks for implementation

State: +